<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    BOV_Score__c Number -> Formula conversion, STEP 1 of 3 (SEVER + DELETE).

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED FOR DEPLOY. The user deploys; this repo only
    describes the change. Companion of destructiveChangesPost.xml in this same
    directory.

    WHY THIS IS AN IN-PLACE DELETE-AND-RECREATE, NOT THE REPO'S USUAL ADDITIVE
    RENAME PATTERN (add -> backfill -> repoint -> retire, see e.g.
    manifest/wave-b-formula/): BOV_Score__c is changing TYPE (Number -> Formula)
    under the SAME API name. A field's type cannot be changed from Number to
    Formula via an update -- Salesforce requires delete + recreate for that
    conversion, and a formula field cannot be created under a name that is still
    occupied by its own soft-deleted predecessor in the Recycle Bin. That is why
    this wave has a genuinely manual step between Step 1 and Step 3 (Setup ->
    Object Manager -> BOV Submission -> Fields & Relationships -> Deleted Fields ->
    BOV_Score__c -> Erase) that no other field-retirement wave in this repo has
    needed. BOV_Score__c is a plain Number field nothing writes (null on every row
    in the org today), so there is no live data to lose and no backfill step.

    THIS PACKAGE (constructive half): the 3 Apex classes that read/order by
    BOV_Score__c, edited to sever every live reference so the field delete below
    is accepted. Each edit is marked "🔴 TEMPORARY — restore in Step 3" inline so
    the restore is mechanical:
      - BovSubmissionSelector.cls  : BOV_Score__c dropped from the SELECT list in
        selectByDispositionId, and from the ORDER BY leg of all three affected
        queries (selectByDispositionId, selectSelectedByDispositionId,
        selectStatusesByDispositionId). CreatedDate ASC, Id ASC remains as the
        tie-break in all three.
      - BovController.cls          : the s.BOV_Score__c.intValue() read in
        getSubmissions replaced with a hardcoded null (the selector no longer
        selects the field, so touching it would throw SObjectException).
      - BovSubmissionSelectorTest.cls : the two now-unreachable BOV_Score__c
        assertions (the populated-field proof and the null-tie premise) removed,
        original text preserved as a restore comment.

    NOT included here and deliberately so, per the task's explicit scope fence:
      - lwc/bovAddResponseModal (renders BOV_Score__c as an editable input) --
        Step 3, because a formula field cannot be written and removing the input
        now would be premature (the field still exists as writable Number until
        the destructive half below runs).
      - layouts/BOV_Submission__c-BOV Submission Layout.layout-meta.xml
        (BOV_Score__c layoutItem, behavior=Edit) -- Step 3, same reasoning; a
        layoutItem referencing a field does not block that field's Metadata API
        deletion (unlike a formula, validation rule, or FlexiPage quick-action
        reference), so there is no ordering dependency forcing this into Step 1.
      - DPEG_Disposition_Edit / DPEG_Disposition_View permission sets (FLS on
        BOV_Score__c) -- not part of this deploy's payload at all; a deleted
        field's FieldPermissions rows are dropped by the platform automatically
        and do not block deletion. Step 3 must still flip
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit's grant back to editable=false before the FORMULA
        recreate (a formula field cannot carry editable=true -- hard deploy
        error) -- see that permission set's own file for the exact prior flip
        history.
      - TestDataFactory.cls -- untouched. Its existing BOV_Score__c removal and
        Asking_Price__c retraction are already correct (concurrent work, see
        the class header); do not revert or blanket-checkout this file.

    Deploy (only once authorised by the user; devops runs a validation-only
    dry-run first per standing project practice):
      sf project deploy start \
        --manifest manifest/bov-score-formula-conversion/package.xml \
        --post-destructive-changes manifest/bov-score-formula-conversion/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
        --target-org usman-dpeg \
        --test-level RunLocalTests --wait 30

    Rollback: the 3 Apex edits are recoverable from git history (this same
    commit modifies them). BOV_Score__c itself is a custom field and therefore
    soft-deleted -- recoverable from the Recycle Bin (Setup -> Object Manager ->
    BOV Submission -> Fields & Relationships -> Deleted Fields -> Restore) up
    until the manual Erase step is performed, after which it is not recoverable
    by any means (a fresh Number field with the same name and zero data would
    have to be created by hand). All rows are null today, so an Erase followed
    by a hand-rebuild loses no data either way.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>BovController</members>
        <members>BovSubmissionSelector</members>
        <members>BovSubmissionSelectorTest</members>
        <name>ApexClass</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
